  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A timely reassessment of conservation status and population baseline for the sumatran rhinoceros in the Ulu Masen Landscape, Aceh Province, Indonesia.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to provide the Government of Indonesia and relevant partners with the most recent status of Sumatran rhinoceros in Ulu Masen as a baseline for a long-term exclusive strategy to secure it in this landscape. This will be done by: (1) conducting a partner meeting and compiling and verifying data to model the most suitable habitats for Sumatran rhino in Ulu Masen; (2) conducting a desktop analysis to produce a predictive map of rhino occurrence; (3) developing a rhino survey protocol and conducting technical training in the implementation of the protocol; (4) carrying out a detection/non-detection rhino field survey; (5) analyzing the field data (using PRESENCE) to obtain unbiased estimates of the factors that influence Sumatran rhino occupancy within the predicted best suitable habitats in the Ulu Masen landscape; and (6) conducting a strategic meeting to formulate future direction of Sumatran rhino conservation the Leuser-Ulu Masen mega landscape.</narrative>
  </description>
